.TH GPGMAN 1 "October 2026" "GPGMan 1.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpgman \- Dual-Style OpenPGP Cryptographic Management Suite (GUI & CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpgman
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B gpgman
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS...\fR]
.br
.B gpgman-cli
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS...\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GPGMan
is a modern, dual-style OpenPGP cryptographic suite providing both a polished
desktop graphical interface built with GTK4 and Libadwaita, and an uncompromising,
headless command-line interface (CLI) with 1:1 functional parity.

Designed for security professionals, sysadmins, and privacy-conscious users, GPGMan
interfaces directly with the active \fBgnupg\fR (GnuPG) backend and its keyrings.
It provides complete lifecycle management for PGP keys, asymmetric and symmetric
encryption/decryption of messages and arbitrary files, digital signature creation
and cryptographic verification, multi-algorithm hashing, and GnuPG daemon diagnostics.

When launched without arguments in a desktop session, or with \fB--gui\fR, GPGMan
opens the GTK4 application. When invoked as \fBgpgman-cli\fR or with any CLI
subcommand, GPGMan executes in headless terminal mode.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --gui
Force launching the graphical user interface (GTK4 / Libadwaita).
.TP
.BR --cli
Force command-line mode even if no subcommand is given.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display available subcommands, command syntax, and usage help.
.TP
.BI --gpg-bin \ PATH
Specify a custom path to the \fBgpg\fR executable.
.TP
.BI --gpg-home \ DIR
Specify an alternate GnuPG home directory (overriding the default \fIGNUPGHOME\fR).

.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS (GUI)
GPGMan's graphical interface includes convenient keyboard accelerators to streamline cryptographic operations:
.TP
.B Enter / Return in Passphrase Rows
When typing a passphrase for symmetric encryption, signing with a protected private key,
or decrypting a message or file, pressing \fBEnter\fR immediately triggers the respective
action (Encrypt or Decrypt) without requiring mouse navigation.
.TP
.B Escape
Dismisses modal dialogs (Key Details, Key Generation, Key Import, About dialog).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quits the application cleanly.

.SH CLI SUBCOMMANDS
.SS Key Management
.TP
.B list-keys
List all public keys in the active keyring along with Key ID, User ID (name, email),
fingerprint, algorithm (RSA, Ed25519), creation date, and expiration status.
.TP
.B list-secret-keys
List only private / secret keys available for signing and decryption.
.TP
.BI generate-key \ [OPTIONS]
Generate a new cryptographic keypair.
.RS
.TP
.BI --name \ NAME
Full name of the keyholder (required).
.TP
.BI --email \ EMAIL
Email address associated with the key (required).
.TP
.BI --comment \ TEXT
Optional comment for the user identity.
.TP
.BI --key-type \ TYPE
Key algorithm: \fBed25519\fR (default, modern and compact) or \fBrsa4096\fR, \fBrsa2048\fR.
.TP
.BI --expire \ DURATION
Expiration duration, e.g. \fB1y\fR (1 year, default), \fB2y\fR, \fB6m\fR, or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.BI --passphrase \ PASS
Passphrase to protect the private key.
.RE
.TP
.BI export-key \ KEY_ID \ [OPTIONS]
Export a public key.
.RS
.TP
.B --armor
Output in ASCII-armored format (\fI-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----\fR). Default is enabled.
.TP
.BI -o ", " --output \ FILE
Save exported key to a file instead of standard output.
.RE
.TP
.BI export-secret-key \ KEY_ID \ [OPTIONS]
Export a private / secret key.
.RS
.TP
.BI --passphrase \ PASS
Passphrase to unlock the private key for export.
.TP
.BI -o ", " --output \ FILE
Destination file path.
.RE
.TP
.BI import-key \ FILE
Import a public key or secret keypair from a file or stdin into the keyring.
.TP
.BI delete-key \ KEY_ID \ [OPTIONS]
Remove a key from the keyring.
.RS
.TP
.B --secret
Delete the secret key rather than the public key.
.TP
.B -y ", " --yes
Skip interactive confirmation.
.RE

.SS Message Cryptography
.TP
.B encrypt-message \ [OPTIONS]
Encrypt a plaintext message into an ASCII-armored PGP block.
.RS
.TP
.BI -r ", " --recipient \ KEY_ID
Recipient public key ID or email. Multiple recipients may be specified.
.TP
.BI -s ", " --sign-with \ KEY_ID
Optionally sign the message with the specified private key.
.TP
.BI --passphrase \ PASS
Passphrase for the signing key (if signing is enabled).
.TP
.B --symmetric
Use passphrase-based symmetric encryption (AES-256) instead of public key cryptography.
.TP
.BI -m ", " --message \ TEXT
Plaintext string. If omitted, input is read from standard input.
.RE
.TP
.B decrypt-message \ [OPTIONS]
Decrypt an ASCII-armored PGP message and verify any embedded signature.
.RS
.TP
.BI --passphrase \ PASS
Passphrase for the secret key or symmetric cipher.
.TP
.BI -m ", " --message \ TEXT
Encrypted text. If omitted, input is read from standard input.
.RE

.SS Digital Signatures & Clearsigning
.TP
.B clearsign-message \ [OPTIONS]
Generate an OpenPGP clearsigned message (\fI-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----\fR).
.RS
.TP
.BI -u ", " --sign-key \ KEY_ID
Signing key ID or email (required).
.TP
.BI --passphrase \ PASS
Passphrase to unlock the signing key.
.TP
.BI -m ", " --message \ TEXT
Message content to sign (or stdin).
.RE
.TP
.B verify-clearsign \ [OPTIONS]
Verify an OpenPGP clearsigned message. Reports signature validity, signer fingerprint,
key ID, and timestamp, and extracts the verified plaintext body.
.RS
.TP
.BI -m ", " --message \ TEXT
Armored clearsigned text (or stdin).
.RE

.SS File Operations
.TP
.B encrypt-file \ [OPTIONS]
Encrypt a file on disk.
.RS
.TP
.BI -i ", " --input \ FILE
Input file path (required).
.TP
.BI -o ", " --output \ FILE
Output encrypted file path (required).
.TP
.BI -r ", " --recipient \ KEY_ID
Recipient key ID (can specify multiple).
.TP
.B --symmetric
Encrypt symmetrically with a passphrase.
.TP
.BI --passphrase \ PASS
Passphrase for symmetric encryption or signing key.
.TP
.B --armor
Create ASCII-armored output (\fI.asc\fR) instead of binary (\fI.gpg\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B decrypt-file \ [OPTIONS]
Decrypt an encrypted file on disk.
.RS
.TP
.BI -i ", " --input \ FILE
Encrypted input file (required).
.TP
.BI -o ", " --output \ FILE
Destination plaintext file (required).
.TP
.BI --passphrase \ PASS
Decryption passphrase if required.
.RE
.TP
.B sign-file \ [OPTIONS]
Sign a file.
.RS
.TP
.BI -i ", " --input \ FILE
File to sign (required).
.TP
.BI -u ", " --sign-key \ KEY_ID
Signing key ID (required).
.TP
.B --detached
Create a detached signature file (\fI.sig\fR or \fI.asc\fR).
.TP
.B --armor
Output in ASCII-armored format.
.RE
.TP
.B verify-file \ [OPTIONS]
Verify a signed file.
.RS
.TP
.BI -i ", " --input \ FILE
Signed file (or data file if using detached signature).
.TP
.BI -s ", " --sig-file \ FILE
Detached signature file (optional for inline-signed files).
.RE

.SS Cryptographic Hashes & System Diagnostics
.TP
.B checksum \ [OPTIONS]
Calculate cryptographic digest of a file.
.RS
.TP
.BI -i ", " --input \ FILE
File to hash.
.TP
.BI -a ", " --algorithm \ ALGO
Hash algorithm: \fBsha256\fR (default), \fBsha512\fR, \fBsha1\fR, or \fBmd5\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B verify-checksum \ [OPTIONS]
Compare a file's hash against an expected value.
.RS
.TP
.BI -i ", " --input \ FILE
Target file.
.TP
.BI -c ", " --hash \ EXPECTED_HASH
Expected hex digest.
.TP
.BI -a ", " --algorithm \ ALGO
Hash algorithm (auto-detected by hash length if omitted).
.RE
.TP
.B system-info
Display GnuPG binary location, version string, active GNUPGHOME, and agent status.
.TP
.B kill-agent
Gracefully terminate running \fBgpg-agent\fR daemon processes to force key cache reload.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B GNUPGHOME
Directory storing GnuPG keyrings, trust databases, and daemon sockets (defaults to \fI~/.gnupg\fR).
.TP
.B GPG_BIN
Path to the \fBgpg\fR binary. If unset, searched in standard system \fIPATH\fR.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/gpgman.1.gz
System manual page for GPGMan.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/gpgman
Primary executable wrapper (launches GUI or CLI depending on arguments).
.TP
.I /usr/bin/gpgman-cli
Dedicated CLI executable symlink.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/gpgman.desktop
XDG desktop entry.
.TP
.I ~/.gnupg/
Default user GnuPG configuration and keyrings.

